Assembler Version 16
====================
Assembled by: version 15 debug build (asm_debug.out with define:enable_debug)

Build notes: The v15 debug build is used because v16 source uses
.ifdef enable_debug conditional compilation, which requires v15 support.
Version 16 also produces both normal and debug builds.

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 15, plus .byte/.word/.asciiz directives,
.reserve, decimal numbers, memory protection, and enhanced conditional
assembly:

Syntax:
- Standard 6502 mnemonic syntax (LDA, STA, etc.)
- All addressing modes (immediate, zero page, absolute, indexed, indirect)
- .data directive for byte/string data (retained for compatibility)
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Decimal constants (parsed by from_decimal.asm)
- Character literals: 'x', '\n', '\\', '\''
- Expression evaluation with +, -, <<, >> operators (left-to-right)
- Quoted strings with full escape sequence support (decode_escape)
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- Optional colon after label definitions (label:)
- Local labels with . prefix
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly with forward reference tracking
- Automatic zero page vs absolute addressing

Directives:
- .include filename - includes contents of another file
- .zeropage - switch to zero page section
- .code - switch to code section
- .data - declare raw byte data (legacy, retained)
- .byte expr [, expr ...] - emit byte values (comma-separated) (new)
- .word expr [, expr ...] - emit 16-bit word values (comma-separated) (new)
- .asciiz expr [, "string" ...] - emit null-terminated strings/values (new)
- .reserve N - reserve N bytes (zero-fill in .code, PC advance in .zeropage) (new)
- .byte / .word (without operand in .zeropage) - allocate zero page storage (new)
- .ifdef label - begin conditional block if label is defined
- .endif - end conditional block
- .macro NAME [param1 param2 ...] - begin macro definition
- .endmacro - end macro definition

Command line:
- Variable argument count
- define:label - pre-define a label
- debug - enable debug output (new)
- small_heap - use reduced heap for testing (new)
- show_captured_macros - display captured macro definitions (new)

Memory protection:
- CHECK_FOR_OUT_OF_MEMORY macro detects heap/stack collision
- 256-byte safety buffer maintained between heap (MEMP16) and
  file stack (FS_P16)

Error handling: reorganized error codes into categories, plus new errors:
- Error codes renumbered and grouped by category ($01-$FF)
- err_too_many_ifdefs ($15): IFDEF_DECISIONS buffer full
- err_macro_nesting_too_deep ($1F): Macro nesting limit exceeded
- err_out_of_memory ($20): Heap/stack collision
- err_token_too_long ($21): Token exceeds buffer
- err_zeropage_overflow ($23): Zero page section overflow
- err_file_not_found ($24): File not found (debug build)
- err_operand_in_zeropage ($25): Operand on .byte/.word in .zeropage
- err_nested_macro_definition ($1B): Nested .macro inside .macro
- Error codes reorganized: usage errors at $F0-$F1, debug at $FE-$FF

New in this version (relative to version 15):
- .byte, .word, .asciiz directives with comma-separated values
  - DATA_MODE tracking (0=.data, 1=.byte, 2=.word, 3=.asciiz)
  - Comma-separated data values in .byte, .word, .asciiz
  - .asciiz auto-appends null terminator after each string
  - Quoted strings supported in .byte and .asciiz
  - .byte/.word without operands in .zeropage allocates storage
- .reserve N directive for reserving bytes
- Decimal number parsing (from_decimal.asm module)
- Memory protection (CHECK_FOR_OUT_OF_MEMORY macro in common.asm)
  - Detects when heap approaches file stack
  - 256-byte safety buffer for indexed addressing
- decode_escape for string escape sequences (\n, \\, \', \0, etc.)
- compare_end_of_token rewritten as positive character class matching
  (alphanumeric + underscore) instead of negative list of terminators
- Error codes reorganized into sequential categories
- macros.asm module with utility macros (SET16, CP16, INC16, etc.)
- Zero page variables use 16-suffix naming (PC16, HEX16, etc.)
- OPERAND16 aliased to HEX16 (single 16-bit location)
- Detailed architecture documentation in source header comments

